Here, $m_1=90 \mathrm{ kg}$ and $m_2=160 \mathrm{ kg}$ Gravitational field intensity due to mass A, $\mathbf{E}_A=\frac{G M_A}{ \mathbf{r}_{C$ A}^2}=$G \frac{90}{\left(3^2\right) }=10 G \hat{\mathbf{r}_{C A} Similarly, \quad \mathbf{E}_B=G \times \frac{160}{4^2}=10 G \hat{\mathbf{r}_{C B}$ In $\triangle A B C, \begin{aligned}
